WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.239 --> 00:00:15.600
Just a few days before Jo was to leave, she received a letter from Beth telling her about

2
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.661
Meg's pregnancy.

3
00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:22.482
Coincidentally it was the Professor who delivered the mail to Jo that day, so she shared the good

4
00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.063
news with him.

5
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:25.803
"I can't believe I'm going to be an aunt!"

6
00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:28.152
she shouted in delight.

7
00:00:28.172 --> 00:00:33.175
For some reason, the idea of Meg getting married had been hard for Jo to accept, but news

8
00:00:33.215 --> 00:00:36.637
that she was going to have a little niece or nephew completely thrilled her.

9
00:00:36.657 --> 00:00:39.698
"You like children, don't you?"

10
00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:40.959
the Professor asked.

11
00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:47.743
Nodding enthusiastically Jo said, "I love their innocence, their curiosity, their energy, and their humor.

12
00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:52.245
That's why if I don't succeed as an author, I am going to become a teacher."

13
00:00:53.246 --> 00:00:57.488
Jo remembered the strange look that the Professor had given her when she made that comment.

14
00:00:58.208 --> 00:01:03.831
He said, "Then perhaps our paths may cross again one day, Jo, because it is my dream to

15
00:01:03.931 --> 00:01:08.354
start a school for boys, and I could use a good teacher like you."

16
00:01:09.615 --> 00:01:14.537
Suddenly feeling shy, Jo merely said, "I didn't realize you had such plans.

17
00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:17.859
One day, I hope you see your dream come true."

18
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.783
Now, as Jo sat packing her bags, she wondered what her dreams were and how they had changed

19
00:01:24.823 --> 00:01:25.844
in these past few months.

20
00:01:26.832 --> 00:01:29.073
A light knock on the door broke into her thoughts.

21
00:01:30.054 --> 00:01:34.236
"Come in if you can find room for your feet," Jo called out, trying to clear some space

22
00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:36.017
among all her belongings scattered everywhere.

23
00:01:36.037 --> 00:01:41.500
"I thought you only had a few things," the Professor joked as he looked around the messy room.

24
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.703
"I guess I must have acquired one or two more things while I was here," Jo said, chuckling.

25
00:01:46.723 --> 00:01:50.205
"Will your bag be able to hold one more small item?"

26
00:01:50.505 --> 00:01:50.906
he asked.

27
00:01:51.586 --> 00:01:54.768
"I'm sure I can find some space somewhere," Jo replied.

28
00:01:55.496 --> 00:01:59.038
"I want to give you this," the Professor said, holding out a wrapped parcel.

29
00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:02.960
Inside was a leather notebook with her initials on the cover.

30
00:02:03.921 --> 00:02:05.562
"Oh, it's beautiful!"

31
00:02:05.922 --> 00:02:06.602
exclaimed Jo.

32
00:02:06.622 --> 00:02:11.265
"For you to record your dreams," the Professor said smiling.

33
00:02:12.085 --> 00:02:15.927
Swallowing the lump in her throat, Jo placed the notebook inside her handbag.

34
00:02:15.947 --> 00:02:21.670
"Also, I want to thank you for this," the Professor said as he took his shoes off and

35
00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.331
proudly wiggled his mended socks.

36
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:25.861
"How did you know?"

37
00:02:26.321 --> 00:02:26.842
laughed Jo.

38
00:02:26.862 --> 00:02:32.066
"When I saw the girls sewing, I knew these stitches belonged to you," he said.

39
00:02:32.967 --> 00:02:34.348
An awkward silence followed.

40
00:02:34.949 --> 00:02:38.191
Then the Professor finally said, "Will you be returning to New York?"

41
00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:43.216
"I would like to, but I can't say with certainty," Jo said honestly.

42
00:02:43.236 --> 00:02:49.221
"I hope we will meet again, Jo March," the Professor said with feeling as he held out his

43
00:02:49.261 --> 00:02:54.749
hand. Smiling as she took his hand, Jo said, "It's been a pleasure knowing you, Fritz."

44
00:02:56.249 --> 00:03:01.771
As Jo finished packing her belongings, Amy was almost done with gathering everything into her luggage.

45
00:03:02.671 --> 00:03:07.112
The following day, she and Aunt March were heading toward their next destination: Italy.

46
00:03:08.172 --> 00:03:12.834
Amy could hardly sleep that night because she had dreamt about visiting Italy since she was a little

47
00:03:12.854 --> 00:03:19.096
girl. "I guess some things do remain the same," she thought, thinking of her longstanding dream to see

48
00:03:19.136 --> 00:03:20.136
that beautiful country.

49
00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:25.163
But Amy had changed in many other ways as she was learning on this trip to Europe.

50
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:32.188
Reflecting on the relationship between Aunt March and Amy's own family, Amy appreciated the worth of close family

51
00:03:32.228 --> 00:03:34.669
ties and the values her parents had taught her.

52
00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.132
She concluded that it was love, not money, that bonded people closely.

53
00:03:40.213 --> 00:03:45.316
That was why she could not marry Fred: she didn't love him, much to the disappointment of Aunt

54
00:03:45.356 --> 00:03:51.625
March. "I have a feeling that something wonderful is waiting for me in Italy," Amy said to herself

55
00:03:51.725 --> 00:03:52.586
as she lay in bed.

56
00:03:53.606 --> 00:03:58.270
Jo's homecoming was so heartwarming that she forgot about her friends in New York for a moment.

57
00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:02.373
"You look different somehow, darling," her mother commented.

58
00:04:02.393 --> 00:04:06.896
"Like a lady," teased her father, playfully touching her stylish bun.

59
00:04:06.916 --> 00:04:12.180
"Mrs. Kirke taught me how to do my hair up in different ways," Jo said proudly.

60
00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.902
"I'm so glad you're home," Beth said quietly.

61
00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.904
"It's as if you never left."

62
00:04:19.068 --> 00:04:23.030
In Jo's eyes though, much had changed during her absence, most notably Beth.

63
00:04:23.951 --> 00:04:29.774
She looked thinner, paler, and lifeless; a total contrast from the sunny, happy girl in Jo's memory.

64
00:04:30.635 --> 00:04:36.198
When Jo told her Mother her worries, Mother shook her head and just said, "She's never really been

65
00:04:36.238 --> 00:04:37.699
the same since the fever."

66
00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.123
Early the next morning, Jo decided to brave the cold and took her new leather notebook and extra

67
00:04:44.143 --> 00:04:45.984
sweater to the pond behind their house.

68
00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:51.254
She was looking forward to having a private moment to reflect upon her trip, but when she got

69
00:04:51.314 --> 00:04:53.455
to the lake, someone was already there.

70
00:04:53.475 --> 00:04:59.337
"Laurie!" she called out excitedly, truly happy to see her best friend.

71
00:04:59.357 --> 00:05:02.518
"Jo! What are you doing here?"

72
00:05:02.779 --> 00:05:03.599
he asked, alarmed.

73
00:05:03.619 --> 00:05:06.540
"I'm back, you know," she laughed.

74
00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.881
"I know," he smiled.

75
00:05:09.521 --> 00:05:11.962
"I was going to come see you later on in the morning."

76
00:05:11.982 --> 00:05:15.784
"I never knew you came down here to the pond," she said.

77
00:05:16.848 --> 00:05:21.049
"I walk down here most mornings," he said, adding, "You don't know everything about me."

78
00:05:21.069 --> 00:05:26.871
"Well, I'm so glad to see you and I have so much to tell you," Jo said, trying

79
00:05:26.891 --> 00:05:30.492
to change the subject because she felt uneasy tension between them.

80
00:05:31.432 --> 00:05:35.353
"So do I, Jo," Laurie said quietly as he stared at her for a long time.

81
00:05:35.373 --> 00:05:41.475
"Laurie, Jo began, thinking she knew what he was about to say but not wanting him to say

82
00:05:41.515 --> 00:05:45.196
it, because once it came out, their friendship would never be the same.

83
00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.621
Laurie abruptly interrupted her.

84
00:05:48.061 --> 00:05:50.862
"This may not be the best time to say this but I don't care.

85
00:05:51.663 --> 00:05:54.164
After you left, my life has been nothing but agony.

86
00:05:55.284 --> 00:05:59.126
I went back to college, and by the way, you'll be happy to know that I received the

87
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:01.527
highest marks in my class and will graduate with honors."

88
00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.528
"That's wonderful, Laurie!

89
00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:04.728
I knew you could do it!

90
00:06:04.888 --> 00:06:10.131
I'm so Congratulating him, Jo prayed she would be able to say a few words before Laurie went

91
00:06:10.271 --> 00:06:12.892
on, but he continued as if he didn't hear her.

92
00:06:14.072 --> 00:06:18.595
"From the first day I met you all those years ago until this very moment, my feelings for

93
00:06:18.615 --> 00:06:21.536
you have never changed and they never will," he said passionately.

94
00:06:22.977 --> 00:06:28.941
Taking her hand, Laurie said, "Jo, my life, no matter how good it is, will never be complete

95
00:06:28.961 --> 00:06:29.781
unless you are in it."

96
00:06:31.342 --> 00:06:36.805
Feeling as though her heart was being broken, Jo somehow found the strength to say what she could

97
00:06:36.925 --> 00:06:37.946
no longer hold back.

98
00:06:38.806 --> 00:06:41.288
"Laurie, please don't do this," she begged him.

99
00:06:41.972 --> 00:06:45.914
"Our friendship is the most precious thing to me, and I don't want it to change.

100
00:06:47.355 --> 00:06:49.597
I can't be the kind of person you want me to be."

101
00:06:51.017 --> 00:06:54.419
Laurie bowed his head, his face crushed with pain.

102
00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.821
"I don't love you like that, Laurie.

103
00:06:57.261 --> 00:06:58.062
I never have,"
